{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes","id":1437635,"title":"Harvesting Gnosis from Banes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-02T08:14:55-08:00","id":1437635,"title":"Harvesting Gnosis from Banes","content":"When a spirit has been reduced to zero Essence shapeshifters can permanently destroy them by harvesting their Gnosis. Has anyone used this option in their games? If so, do you check the character for Wyrm taint when doing this to a bane or do anything similar? My headcannon is that the characters can harvest up to the spirit's Gnosis rating is gnosis points. If they harvest at least half of them the spirit is permanently destroyed. If they harvest less than half it is crippled when it comes out of slumber and is severely angry at the offender.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for expanding on this option are greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T08:46:30-08:00","id":1437638,"title":"","content":"Yes, we use it frequently in our LARP game.<br /> Yes, and there is usually taint there.<br /> In our LARP game garou can harvest half the spirits Gnosis rating, at a rate of one per round. Contact is needed and in the most cases consumption of the spirit's body (although this might not be applicable to, let's say, wind spirits).<br /> We never thought about what happens if a garou didn't consume all Gnosis, but from the top of my head the spirit's body would lie there until the scene ends and then Reform, if not all Gnosis was taken. If the spirit doesn't possess the Reform charm, possibly other predatory spirits might kill the wounded spirit of, or it might Slumber there until Essence returns (which might be a long time, if the spirits essence is not found at that place).<br /> <br /> Englings, in our game, have only one Gnosis to give and die happily if killed outside of the Sacred Hunt Rite. With the Rite all Gnosis of a hunters in restored. We have a public list where players mark of Englings their character hunted near the caern (the primary game location). The list also informs how long a player has to leave the game to hunt one Gnosis (meaning one Engling). So, there is a line for 10 Minutes with 6 boxes to check. Then a line for 15 minutes/10 boxes and a line for 20 minutes with 12 boxes and so on. The times and boxes vary from game to game, depending on the Moot in the previous game and how much the Gnosis 'gifted' into the Moot Rite exceeded the required minimum.<br /> It's also affected by a longrunning plot we run, involving Weaver agents mapping migration of Englings and poisoning them to dry out the spiritual energy in the region, making Englings more time-consuming to find...<br /> We generally ignore the &quot;urban engling&quot; and it's stats (from Book of the City) and only use the Englings and their chraracteristics in the game...<br /> <br /> In game, Theurges have debated if it is okay to permanently kill banes for they are part of Creation and permanently killing them might upset some balance. But consenus today is, that a bane isn't really defeated until killed. The &quot;tainted&quot; Gnosis gained often leads to shortterm character quirks, thematically tied to the type of bane responsible.<br /> <br /> Killing other spirits is frowned upon and rarely happens, but would be the way to go, if a garou in frenzy beats a spirit into slumber and has no new target, meaning he is continuing to deal damage to the spirit....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 03-02-2021, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T10:01:46-08:00","id":1437646,"title":"","content":"Other than the brief mention in the Spirits in Combat section, is harvesting Gnosis in this way ever addressed in the rules or other sourcebooks? I admit I have overlooked this section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T11:18:35-08:00","id":1437661,"title":"","content":"@heinrich: thank you very much - that is good information.<br /> <br /> @Black Fox: that mention in the Spriits in Combat section is the only one of which I am aware. It was similar in earlier editions - an almost throw-away line with nothing to support it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T11:29:16-08:00","id":1437663,"title":"","content":"Thanks for clarifying that. I am usually a detailed reader or text and notice things others ignore, but I completely overlooked this. I'll start including this in my chronicles. It answers a lot of questions - &quot;how can we permanently destroy Banes&quot; is an ongoing player concern. But I'll need to figure what approach I like in terms of how much Gnosis can be harvested, if any rolls are required, and how to handle the flavor text. And that leads directly to your post!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T12:56:16-08:00","id":1437680,"title":"","content":"I'd love to hear what you come up with. Heinrich's LARP rules sound good for that setting and having input from the tabletop setting would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T13:20:43-08:00","id":1437685,"title":"","content":"The main concerns that appear to me is that 1) this may be too much a source of ready Gnosis, and that 2) there should not be a 100% ease of permanently destroying Banes as a result. Once it is implemented that by harvesting Gnosis of defeated Banes, every PC is going to do so. It either becomes something assumed to happen in the game (boring), or has a chance of failure (a little more interesting).<br /> <br /> I like Heinrich's LARP rules that it is limited to half the Gnosis trait of the spirit, and that the harvest is limited to one per round. I also believe the Garou need to be at the physical proximity in the Umbra where the spirit was &quot;slain&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I think we need to figure out how quickly the spirit fades away (are there rules for this?). And I think there needs to be some mechanic to determine how much harvesting can occur in that time. Roll well and the spirit is destroyed and all Gnosis harvested. Roll poor and the spirit fades away before all Gnosis is harvested (though some may be partially harvested). This should be easy to adjudicate so the game can move on. But what trait or traits to use? The difficulty to roll against? And what would multiple successes mean?<br /> <br /> Also need to decide if more than one Garou can harvest the same spirit at the same time. If so, it is limited to something like a pack stepping sideways using the Opener of the Way rules. So you have to be part of the same pack to do so, but Garou from other packs can't. This may impact the above roll by decreasing its difficulty or increasing the rate of harvest.<br /> <br /> And if Garou can destroy spirits by harvesting Gnosis, then other spiritual creatures should be able to as well. Other Changing Breeds, and spirits as well as Black Spiral Dancers. Perhaps even Fomori who have Gnosis or other umbral powers. So we need to determine how often do these creatures harvest Gnosis from Gaian spirits? This is more of a setting issue. Should BSDs or other enemies be constantly defeating and harvesting spirits? Or do we want that to be left for special story purposes? It impacts the depiction of the setting, and would influence the response of Garou.<br /> <br /> Also, what about spirits not from the Middle Umbra? But wraiths and plasmic creatures from the Dark Umbra, or astral spirits from the High Umbra? I think the best thing would be to say that this does not happen. Even if such creatures possibly have a Gnosis trait (Astral spirits do, but wraiths and plasmics do not), I would say they are too different for Middle Umbra creatures to do. I am bringing this up only to be a completionist because otherwise the issue will come up.<br /> <br /> I'll have to ponder on this more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T02:46:43-08:00","id":1437778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1437685#post1437685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main concerns that appear to me is that 1) this may be too much a source of ready Gnosis, and that 2) there should not be a 100% ease of permanently destroying Banes as a result. Once it is implemented that by harvesting Gnosis of defeated Banes, every PC is going to do so. It either becomes something assumed to happen in the game (boring), or has a chance of failure (a little more interesting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the LARP game, we have short term derangements of sorts as a drawback.<br /> If the fight is part of a longer campaign, also the taint makes most uses of &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; meaningless until a &quot;Rite of Cleansing&quot; can be performed.<br /> Also, we have some spawns of larger banes, that do not allow to for gnosis harvest.<br /> <br /> But, you are right, in umbral fights regaining Gnosis is usually easy for the PCs.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to have harvesting automatically killing a bane (or be successful for that matter), make it a roll. Each round the PC rolls Gnosis against the Gnosis of the bane. Each uneven success gets him a Gnosis and harvests one of the bane's Gnosis. But, also the Bane is allowed to roll Gnosis and reform eventually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1437685#post1437685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think we need to figure out how quickly the spirit fades away (are there rules for this?). And I think there needs to be some mechanic to determine how much harvesting can occur in that time. Roll well and the spirit is destroyed and all Gnosis harvested. Roll poor and the spirit fades away before all Gnosis is harvested (though some may be partially harvested). This should be easy to adjudicate so the game can move on. But what trait or traits to use? The difficulty to roll against? And what would multiple successes mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>My suggestion for the mechanics if the Spirit has &quot;Re-Form&quot; (why is the Charm entry with a '-'. All the spirit stats are copy&amp;paste from other sources and don't have a dash. Is it to troll people using PDF search?)<br /> <br /> The &quot;fading&quot; has no time given in my recollection, but it should not be in the scope of rounds, imo. Especially since garou are seemingly able to harvest bane bodyparts for ritual sacrifice or fetish creation (Fang dagger). So, I see it happen, when a scene ends, after minutes.<br /> Re-Form is said to take a full round. Is that D&amp;D talk? Meaning, I roll now but reform when it would be my turn again?<br /> Obviously, no rules are given if the process is stopped if the bane is attacked or even slain (but not harvested) in the meantime...<br /> Does this mean, a bane can't split dicepools to Re-Form and dodge?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1437685#post1437685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also need to decide if more than one Garou can harvest the same spirit at the same time. If so, it is limited to something like a pack stepping sideways using the Opener of the Way rules. So you have to be part of the same pack to do so, but Garou from other packs can't. This may impact the above roll by decreasing its difficulty or increasing the rate of harvest.</div> </div> </div> </div>We allow for multiple garou to harvest the gnosis. There is an obvious limit, for players have to step next to the NPC actor, who is either cowering or lying on the ground when defeated. Usually, there is only one garou feeding from the spirit/bane, though.<br /> <br /> In most cases, garou will point out a bane that is lying on the battlefield and can be harvested to theurges in their group. They need the gnosis to fuel &quot;mother's touch&quot;. Also, if the bane NPC actors hands out tokens with each Gnosis harvested (to determine the severity of the short term derangements), they are often put into relation to permanent Gnosis scores, so theurges are on average less affected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1437685#post1437685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if Garou can destroy spirits by harvesting Gnosis, then other spiritual creatures should be able to as well. Other Changing Breeds, and spirits as well as Black Spiral Dancers. Perhaps even Fomori who have Gnosis or other umbral powers. So we need to determine how often do these creatures harvest Gnosis from Gaian spirits? This is more of a setting issue. Should BSDs or other enemies be constantly defeating and harvesting spirits? Or do we want that to be left for special story purposes? It impacts the depiction of the setting, and would influence the response of Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fera should absolutely be able to do so, as should BSD, obviously. Mages have their own rules. Fomori, maybe, if they have adequate powers.<br /> <br /> In our LARP we use my favorit approach that spirits are rare in the umbrascape of the penumbra. So, running about and trying to slai and harvest gaffelings just isn't as much an impact as toremting/torturing/killing humans or other things a BSD could do. However, especially a fallen garou who has some knowledge about the garou of a sept could use the Rite of Summoning to summon the pack totem avatar of a specific pack, attack and permanently kill it. There are no clear rules what a garou needs to know to summon a specific spirlt (But 'naming the spirit' should work, as well as possibly some parapernalia). This certainly is a plot, not an everyday's means of BSDvsGarou combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1437685#post1437685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what about spirits not from the Middle Umbra? But wraiths and plasmic creatures from the Dark Umbra, or astral spirits from the High Umbra? I think the best thing would be to say that this does not happen. Even if such creatures possibly have a Gnosis trait (Astral spirits do, but wraiths and plasmics do not), I would say they are too different for Middle Umbra creatures to do. I am bringing this up only to be a completionist because otherwise the issue will come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. We rarely come into this in our LARP, though.<br /> Also, even an enchanted garou should not be able to harvest Gnosis form Chimera <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 03-03-2021, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T04:09:22-08:00","id":1437787,"title":"","content":"This was always a bit of a stickler in our games. For most players the idea of getting Wyrm taint was enough not to resort to this casually. However, we did discuss it as an option, and we concluded that you could only attempt that on a Spirit with lower gnosis than yours, and that it would involve a contested roll between your gnosis and theirs and you could harvest the net successes from the Spirit you're killing. Afterwards you would experience strong emotions and dreams connected to the bane you devoured for a number of days equal to its gnosis, and you would have to keep performing rites of cleansing through that period and be monitored for how sane you are.<br /> <br /> So it's more sin eating, and less Gnosis Buffet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T11:08:45-08:00","id":1437833,"title":"","content":"Those are some nice ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T19:53:55-08:00","id":1438225,"title":"","content":"I had no idea this was an option without the Ghost Eating Technique Gift (in CB20). So what's the difference between doing it this way for free, vs. learning and using that Gift?<br /> <br /> But I think the Theurges' concerns are legit. Reformation, reincarnation, and rebirth are the natural cycles of the Triat. Death caused by the Balance Wyrm always led to rebirth of some kind. Permanently destroying something forever may be unnatural. It's probably necessary with the unbalanced, unnatural situation of the World of Darkness, but it should still have serious spiritual repercussions for the Garou (and Fera) who do it often, or repeatedly, for a while. Essentially, instead of letting the Bane reform, they are incorporating that Bane's essence and perversion into their own souls. Maybe Grondr could do this without any spiritual peril, but they're extinct.<br /> <br /> That said, as for the ecological or cosmic repercussions of consuming those Banes... well which is better? To [help the Weaver] keep the Wyrm bound, or to destroy pieces of it? The one probably strengthens the Weaver's grip on the cosmos. The other... might strengthen the Balance Wyrm? Or maybe it actually strengthens the Defiler? The last emotions of the Bane as it's spiritually devoured probably go somewhere... and do ... something.<br /> <br /> Obviously, if they do this to Gaian or Wyld Spirits, it would probably screw up the local spirit world. The novel Breathe Deeply mentioned that removing large numbers of natural spirits from the local Umbra all at once damages the spiritual and physical ecosystem. And it pisses off the local spirits, up to Incarnae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-05-2021, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:57:26-08:00","id":1438239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438225#post1438225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had no idea this was an option without the Ghost Eating Technique Gift (in CB20).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I completely overlooked this and until now never heard anyone mention this. And ThomasM is right. This has been in every edition of the game, but very easy to overlook. I just looked in my copy of the first edition corebook. It's right there, albeit in different form to reflect the rules back then.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;A Garou who reduces a spirit's Power to 0 may also elect to take up to five points of Gnosis from the spirit in order to recharge his own Gnosis (this kills the spirit if it has less than six Gnosis); this is a good way to make lots of spirits very angry, however.&quot;</i> - Werewolf: the Apocalypse (1st edition), pg 157.<br /> <br /> This has some important restrictions that I think would be good to incorporate into people's own rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438225#post1438225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think the Theurges' concerns are legit. Reformation, reincarnation, and rebirth are the natural cycles of the Triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>There should definitely be some consequences as spirits react negatively to you. At least if you harvest enough Gnosis to actually destroy the spirit.<br /> <br /> As I see it there are two basic approaches. First, killing any spirit (including Banes) angers ALL spirits because that is just how they are. Second, it depends on the type of spirit you destroy, and the type of spirits who are angered by that. I think either approach can be justified, but each has their own consequences in game.<br /> <br /> For my own chronicles, I am thinking about going with the second approach and using these groups to generate different reactions.<br /> <br /> 1) Gaian spirits<br /> 2) Corrupted Gaian spirits<br /> 3) &quot;Normal&quot; Banes/Triatic Spirits<br /> 3) Truly alien Bane spirits<br /> <br /> From a Garou perspective, you don't destroy Gaian spirits ever. You will anger all your natural spirit allies including pack, caern, and tribal totems.<br /> <br /> You also don't destroy corrupted Gaian spirits either. Those can always be redeemed, and can still be filling an important role for Gaia. However, the rare and exceptional destruction might be overcome with appropriate contrition and chiminage. Likewise for BSDs, they would anger Bat or Whippoorwill or other spirits by destroying Gaian spirits, because those could be corrupted. There is still some affinity.<br /> <br /> Then there are ordinary Triatic Spirits: spirits like Pattern Spiders, Sparks, Scrags. They serve important metaphysical functions outside/above the Gaian Realm. Gaian spirits might not care if such high level spirits are destroyed, but Triatic Spirits sense a kinship with each other even if not an allegiance. Destroying one of them won't affect a spirit of one of the other groups, but among the Triatic spirit category you will piss them all off as their danger senses go off.<br /> <br /> By truly alien Banes I mean things that clearly are not part of Earth's order. These would be bizarre Deep Umbral spirits or similar out of place spirits that should not be on Gaia. I would put Nexus Crawlers here. These could be destroyed and not anger other spirits. Maybe upset other Wyrm spirits to lesser degrees.<br /> <br /> This is just my current thoughts, and they may not be what I go with. So I am very open to changing my mind. Other people might prefer a greater or lesser number of types, and different levels of notoriety for doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T00:15:07-08:00","id":1438274,"title":"","content":"My guess is, that the 'Ghost Eating Technique' Gift was written by someone, who also didn't realise the ability to destroy spirits, who were defeated, was already present. Or, it was realised, which is why the Gift has additional usage against wraiths and possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T08:22:16-08:00","id":1438315,"title":"","content":"I reread Ghost-Eating Technique. It only gains the character 1-3 Gnosis, but it allows the user to defeat spirits faster than they could otherwise, and guarantees the spirit is permanently destroyed regardless of how much Gnosis or Essence it had. It also makes no mention of taint from ghost-eating a Bane or Spectre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T11:40:16-08:00","id":1438343,"title":"","content":"Well, taint is a difficult thing. If you do something that generates taint, the taint is on you, the place the deed is performed and the vicitim, as well as possibly tools used. So, killing people should taint the person doing it, regardless of the person being a psychopathic miller, a soldier in combat or a garou. It also doesn't make a difference who the dead people were.<br /> The difference in these scenarios is how the taint dissipates again. For garou part-taking in Rites and especially Rites of Cleansing and Moots is important to remove taint. Which is why it usually doesn't accumulate - which is a danger to, for example, Ronin.<br /> <br /> So, destroying a spirit, even banes or spectres, might bring forth taint in any case. But, it might not be a big deal after all....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T15:26:04-08:00","id":1438376,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't agree that killing automatically generates taint. Garou (and several kinds of Fera) are made for killing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:18:40-08:00","id":1438389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438376#post1438376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't agree that killing automatically generates taint. Garou (and several kinds of Fera) are made for killing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this depends on who and why you kill. You can easily get tainted by killing people who didn't have it coming or who were bystanders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438274#post1438274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess is, that the 'Ghost Eating Technique' Gift was written by someone, who also didn't realise the ability to destroy spirits, who were defeated, was already present. Or, it was realised, which is why the Gift has additional usage against wraiths and possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone really liked Exalted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:32:21-08:00","id":1438392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438389#post1438389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this depends on who and why you kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, and that is exactly what I do not think.<br /> I would think, that the who and why play a role in how quickly the taint fades (among other factors) but the act itself will create the taint in any case.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:49:34-08:00","id":1438395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438392#post1438392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, and that is exactly what I do not think.<br /> I would think, that the who and why play a role in how quickly the taint fades (among other factors) but the act itself will create the taint in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that make every garou by default though? They're normal state has them killing fomori, wyrm spirits, and other such creatures on mass. If killing alone is wyrmish, then werewolves become pointless and contradictory as their main mode for fighting the wyrm ends up feeding it instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T17:00:47-08:00","id":1438397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438395#post1438395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that make every garou by default though? They're normal state has them killing fomori, wyrm spirits, and other such creatures on mass. If killing alone is wyrmish, then werewolves become pointless and contradictory as their main mode for fighting the wyrm ends up feeding it instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>But taint on people, things and places isn't feeding the Wyrm, necessarily. Especially if you kill (and therefore stop permanently) minions of the wyrm you come out with less wyrmishness in total.<br /> Killing, being killed and dying are inherently natural things. It is predominantly the corruption that is around since the Wyrm got mad that is bad for the balance as a whole. And while wyrm taint that isn't dissipating, cleansed or otherwise negated, but rather added to and accumulation, might corrupt a person, thing or place, it normally is not doing so in the short term...<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> &quot;Sense Wyrm isn't 'Detect Evil'&quot; (a sidebar in the Storyteller's Handbook, iirc) and, iirc, the WoD: Outcasts Ronin section, detailing that regular participation in Rites as an underlining positive effects on the garou that Ronin miss out on, are indicators for my opinion on the matter as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 03-06-2021, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T17:49:42-08:00","id":1438405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438397#post1438397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But taint on people, things and places isn't feeding the Wyrm, necessarily. Especially if you kill (and therefore stop permanently) minions of the wyrm you come out with less wyrmishness in total.<br /> Killing, being killed and dying are inherently natural things. It is predominantly the corruption that is around since the Wyrm got mad that is bad for the balance as a whole. And while wyrm taint that isn't dissipating, cleansed or otherwise negated, but rather added to and accumulation, might corrupt a person, thing or place, it normally is not doing so in the short term...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then wouldn't permanently killing a bane be similar? If killing something wyrmish ultimately reduces the net amount of wyrm taint, then killing a bane shouldn't be a big deal and maybe require a rite of cleansing afterward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438397#post1438397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT:<br /> &quot;Sense Wyrm isn't 'Detect Evil'&quot; (a sidebar in the Storyteller's Handbook, iirc) and, iirc, the WoD: Outcasts Ronin section, detailing that regular participation in Rites as an underlining positive effects on the garou that Ronin miss out on, are indicators for my opinion on the matter as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, W20 says this blatently, but being evil and Contributing to evil are different things. It may not be &quot;Detect Evil&quot;, but it is &quot;Detect Wyrm&quot;.<br /> <br /> Pentex employees aren't necessarily evil. They're just average people that, as far as they know, are working normal jobs in a normal business. The problem is that Pentex destroys the world and furthers the Wyrms goals regardless of what their employees want. That's why Pentex employees read as wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> That's the thing though. If any killing ultimately feeds the wyrm, then the garou nations habit of accomplishing its goals by killing and/or destroying wyrmish things ultimately serves the wyrm's purposes even if they ideologically oppose it. Thus the garou should read as wyrm tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T18:07:11-08:00","id":1438408,"title":"","content":"Ingesting Wyrm Essence straight from the source. What could <i>possibly</i> go wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T18:56:14-08:00","id":1438418,"title":"","content":"If all killing is wrong, where do you stop? The WoD does not have a clear line between sapient beings with souls and nonsapient beings who are only good for food. So is it Wyrm-tainted to kill a rabbit and eat it? It had a sleeping spirit and a family and a natural role in the ecosystem. Its ghost went to the Bush of Ghosts or became an animal Plasmic. Are all wild predators inherently Wyrm tainted then?<br /> <br /> I really think you should consider the difference between the Balance Wyrm and the Triatic Wyrm. Wyrm taint only concerns the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T23:32:22-08:00","id":1438441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438405#post1438405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then wouldn't permanently killing a bane be similar? If killing something wyrmish ultimately reduces the net amount of wyrm taint, then killing a bane shouldn't be a big deal and maybe require a rite of cleansing afterward.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the garou doing the deed, in regards to Wyrm Taint, yes.<br /> <br /> There is however an argument there, that the amount of Wyrmishness is relatively high and relatively pure. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12219\" data-vbnamecard=\"12219\">Demigod Beast</a> said, &quot;What could go wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> That is why we, in the LARP game have short term derangements, if the amount of Gnosis ingested is &quot;large&quot; in relation to the permanent Gnosis of the character....<br /> <br /> There was, some years back, an discussion among theurges, if banes aren't just as much part of Gaias design as any other spirit and that destroying them completely may be upsetting some balance. Another argument was, that Gaia only intended Englings to be sacrificed in that order. It was an philosophical, metaphsysical, in-game argument that ultimately didn't concern most garou and didn't change the practice of collecting Gnosis from banes, without any repercussions to renown. That is, unless their consumation of wyrmish Gnosis isn't so excessive that the following derangements lead to them doing harm to others...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438405#post1438405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, W20 says this blatently, but being evil and Contributing to evil are different things. It may not be &quot;Detect Evil&quot;, but it is &quot;Detect Wyrm&quot;.<br /> <br /> Pentex employees aren't necessarily evil. They're just average people that, as far as they know, are working normal jobs in a normal business. The problem is that Pentex destroys the world and furthers the Wyrms goals regardless of what their employees want. That's why Pentex employees read as wyrm tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It is &quot;detect wyrm taint&quot;. As I wrote, revised ST Handbook (iirc) states the taint will be on offender, tools, places and victims of a wyrmish deed. So, garou have to investigate still to find who is to blame and how to stop it. That's where &quot;Scent of the true Form&quot; and &quot;Truth of Gaia&quot; come in, and some other Gifts like them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438405#post1438405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing though. If any killing ultimately feeds the wyrm, then the garou nations habit of accomplishing its goals by killing and/or destroying wyrmish things ultimately serves the wyrm's purposes even if they ideologically oppose it. Thus the garou should read as wyrm tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, directly after a savage battle, they should. But like I wrote, their way of live and their usage of Rites will make the taint go away relatively fast and will usually prevent it turning into corruption (although fallen garou aren't unheard of).<br /> There exclusion from Gaian Rites is, according to WoD:Outcasts Ronin section a great problem for the Ronins. It is also the reason the book introduces morality and a system akin to vampires Humanity explicitly for Ronin. Other garou in general aren't in danger and falling to the wyrm (as a PC) isn't part of WtA's core themes, but if you play a Ronin centric game, the authors thought it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T23:38:29-08:00","id":1438442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438418#post1438418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all killing is wrong, where do you stop? The WoD does not have a clear line between sapient beings with souls and nonsapient beings who are only good for food. So is it Wyrm-tainted to kill a rabbit and eat it? It had a sleeping spirit and a family and a natural role in the ecosystem. Its ghost went to the Bush of Ghosts or became an animal Plasmic. Are all wild predators inherently Wyrm tainted then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is for the ST to decide and set the mood of the game.<br /> Eating the rabbit after killing it certainly is different that catering one's sardistic tendencies by setting a rabbit on fire while still alive, right?<br /> A fox killing all hens due to rabies might also be different than just killing them to eat.<br /> There is certainly a lot of things that might generate neglectable amounts of taint. As long as they don't accumulate they are perfectly normal and part of Gaias design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438418#post1438418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think you should consider the difference between the Balance Wyrm and the Triatic Wyrm. Wyrm taint only concerns the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the point. The Gift doesn't make that distinction.It is for the gaou to put brainpower into what the Gift registered (or get clues for additional successes).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T07:41:08-08:00","id":1438463,"title":"","content":"I just don't recall any book saying that Wyrm taint is caused by eating or hunting. I think that is a change you've made.<br /> <br /> If <b>everything</b> associated with the Balace Wyrm causes taint, then that includes weeding the garden, destroying inanimate objects, feeling any emotion associated with an Urge Wyrm even at healthy levels, and maybe even feeling Rage. The Balance Wyrm is one third of all possible activities on Earth.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling not to say something that looks like a <i>reductio ad absurdem</i> attack because the consequences would be colossal. Every predatory animal on Earth, maybe <b>all</b> animals, would reek of the Wyrm constantly, because none of them use Gaian rites. Every human being would reek of the Wyrm, indiscriminately, as though they were fomori. Even fire might inherently stink of the Wyrm. It would make the Gift useless. Why would Gaia, or the spirits, give them such a misleading and useless Gift? When the Gift is made useless by being surrounded by Wyrm taint (such as in Malfeas) the books explicitly call this out. The W20 Book of the Wyrm and some other books have Pentex deliberately spreading small amounts of Wyrm taint around to confuse the Garou and ruin the use of this Gift in particular - something they wouldn't bother with if all animals and humans everywhere were already tainted all the time.<br /> <br /> No book mentions any Garou saying &quot;Yeah all hunting and killing causes Wyrm taint, so we are all tainted.&quot; or &quot;Yeah, but all predators are of the Wyrm, so clearly that isn't a bad thing.&quot; Nobody is said to need a Rite of Cleansing after catching an evening meal. Some Garou worry that Rage is of the Wyrm, but they don't worry that eating a rabbit makes them spiritually unclean. On the contrary, hunting is natural and correct, and showing respect to one's prey makes it spiritually clean.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, combatting the Wyrm &quot;wherever it dwells and wherever it breeds&quot; would be untenable if all wolves and humans everywhere were inherently of the Wyrm and accumulated Wyrm taint at every meal. That tenet of the Litany clearly refers to the Triatic Wyrm, but if the Garou can't tell the difference between Balance and Corruption, it would be unenforceable, at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-07-2021, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T11:47:36-08:00","id":1438485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438463#post1438463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <b>everything</b> associated with the Balace Wyrm causes taint, then that includes weeding the garden, destroying inanimate objects, feeling any emotion associated with an Urge Wyrm even at healthy levels, and maybe even feeling Rage. The Balance Wyrm is one third of all possible activities on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, but if the amount of taint and duration it lasts is neglectable, like I wrote, then there really isn't a problem.<br /> <br /> If one theurge really, really wanted to know if the fox killing the hen generates taint, and he boosts all relevant stats with temporary bonuses from spirit pacts and talens and gifts and spends a willpower for automatic success and scores 11+ successes on a roll made in the very moment the fox delivers the killing bite, then sure, there is taint for him to detect on the fox, the hen and the place of the killing.<br /> A moment later the taint is gone already - so most garou will never know or care.<br /> <br /> The taint would only accumulate if conditions are right. Also, the amount of killing an enemy in combat is probably a lot larger that hunting a hen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438463#post1438463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Gift is made useless by being surrounded by Wyrm taint (such as in Malfeas) the books explicitly call this out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Malfeas or, let's say, just the next city?<br /> Storytellers Handbook page 85:<br /> <i>Players who rely too heavily on the Sense Wyrm Gift to discern between \u201cevil and needs to be killed\u201d and \u201cnot evil and should be protected\u201d are SOL in the city. Wyrm-taint is a pervasive spiritual force, and it clings to victims as well as abusers, the violated as well as the violator. Although certainly not everyone in a city is going to smell of the Wyrm, using Sense Wyrm in any crowded area will probably register multiple instances of taint.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438463#post1438463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The W20 Book of the Wyrm and some other books have Pentex deliberately spreading small amounts of Wyrm taint around to confuse the Garou and ruin the use of this Gift in particular - something they wouldn't bother with if all animals and humans everywhere were already tainted all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, what they spread is probably a factor 1000 less then a BSD would have, but still a factor 1000 more than an animal would cause, when hunting...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438463#post1438463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No book mentions any Garou saying &quot;Yeah all hunting and killing causes Wyrm taint, so we are all tainted.&quot; [...] Nobody is said to need a Rite of Cleansing after catching an evening meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then gain, there is the &quot;Prayer for the Prey&quot;. Combined with page 61 of WoD: Outcasts it is suggested that participation in Garou rites in general help to ward of taint that might eventually become corruption.<br /> <br /> So, if you take what I write and apply it in an absurd way, that is obviously contra to the way the world is described, then <i>Reductio ad absurdum</i> to discard it makes sense - but that is not what I wrote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T10:26:14-08:00","id":1438767,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a massive difference between \u2018killing\u2019 a Bane and <i>eating a Bane</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T11:19:02-08:00","id":1438779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438767#post1438767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a massive difference between \u2018killing\u2019 a Bane and <i>eating a Bane</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between reducing a bane to zero Essence/Power, and killing it permanently.<br /> <br /> &quot;Harvesting Gnosis&quot; is the way to kill it permanently. There is no definitive description, how this happens in the game world:<br /> - Do garou meditate near the bane and harvest the gnosis through an act of concentration and wishful thinking?<br /> - Do they tear through the banes ephermal body, while chanting, hoping to find a magical gem that is the physical representation of the Gnosis to be harvested?<br /> <br /> We don't know.<br /> The common believe my LARP troupe developed over the last 20 years is, that the body of a spirit/bane needs to be consumed (at least partially) to harvest the gnosis. If the spirit/bane is of a type that makes this impossible or unbelievable then concentration and a physical contact with the spirit's/bane's body is required.<br /> <br /> But, in general, in a lot of fantasy, and real world mysticism consumption is a means of metaphysical taking possession of metaphysical energy. Eating an enemies heart or Christian last supper ceremonies are examples.<br /> <br /> You could argue that there is a massive difference between killing it permanently and eating it, but really, what is the difference?<br /> That the garou aren't hungry anymore?<br /> When we define the eating as the means of harvesting the Gnosis and therefore killing the bane and we don't attribute any effects to the act that we wouldn't also attribute to &quot;harvesting Gnosis&quot;, then there isn't really a difference. Especially, since no alternatives are described on how &quot;harvesting Gnosis&quot; works. But unlike a table top game where someone states, &quot;I harvest the banes Gnosis and therefore kill it&quot; and the ST replies &quot;fine&quot; in a LARP game there needs to be consensus on what happens through gestures and physical display of action that work ideally without additional verbal description. That is acting like one was why eating the spirit/bane works well to portray the harvesting of Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 03-09-2021, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T13:08:49-08:00","id":1438795,"title":"","content":"....Grondr did that, and the Garou wiped them out, because of it. And you regain Gnosis from caerns and englings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T01:23:18-08:00","id":1438907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437635-harvesting-gnosis-from-banes?p=1438795#post1438795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....Grondr did that, and the Garou wiped them out, because of it. And you regain Gnosis from caerns and englings.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we started our LARP revised core had just come out and there wasn't a German translation yet. Gondr background, didn't exist, but the harvesting from spirits/banes was around since 1st Edition as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> pointed out.<br /> <br /> Also, you get Gnosis from Meditation and Englings (and Rites and Gifts), but not from Caerns. As has been pointed out in this topic, too, iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T12:00:24-07:00","id":1439866,"title":"","content":"Heinrich I did not understand the emphasis you were putting on Balance Wyrm taint being just a momentary blip. I'm still not sure I understand what you are saying, especially how this taint goes away without any intervention, but it looks less untenable now that you explained it more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T02:08:16-07:00","id":1439985,"title":"","content":"Well, there wasn't really any mention that events one could attribute to the balance wyrm or the natural order would not generate taint and that the taint would be different from wyrm taint that is the result of corrupted wyrm. For the whole sense Wyrm/Wyld/Weaver Gift mechanic and the various taints to work in a meaningful way it seemed there are two approaches.<br /> <br /> Either there are events/actions that happen every day that don't lead to taint or there is taint caused by any suitable event, but it either doesn't last long or is small in magnitude.<br /> <br /> To my tasted the first option isn't satisfying and I can't really bring it to work with the way for example taint in cities is described. My co-STs in my LARP game concurred.<br /> <br /> So, to us, it made sense that wyrm taint, or any taint for that matter, is spread over a large scale, with rather fine quantities for events of (subjective) smaller scope to events with graver impacts causing more taint. More taint being not a linear thing, but rather logarithmic, so magnitudes more taint. With this approach we could make more sense of how taint comes to be.<br /> <br /> It also makes sense that taint isn't permanent. WoD: Outcasts' take on Ronin and garou Rites for us is the reason why garou usually do not accumulate taint to horrendous amounts. From there we extrapolated that any person should decrease taint with time and spirituality of some (appropriate) sort. Obviously, belonging to a wyrm cult should not lead to decrease in taint <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But, a boy who had brawl with another boy in school, accidentally pushing that boy down the stairs and killing him should not necessarily have wyrm taint when he is a dedicated social worker in his forties. Places and objects aren't sentient, so we don't think they can live spiritual lives, so time alone will dissipate taint, although part-taking in events that in essence would be counter-acting the taint would reduce it. That's what your garden variety Feng Shui counsellor might do, even if he doesn't have hedge magic.<br /> <br /> In the end, we dodge the question &quot;why do some actions cause taint and others do?&quot; by saying &quot;All events cause taint, the amount and time you can detect is just varies - depending on circumstances and successes you rolled&quot;. An answer that gives us much more freedom and saves us from out of game discussions and continuity errors.<br /> &quot;When Bob STed four years ago, we came to a scene where a boy pushed someone down the stairs a day earlier and there was taint. My character detected it. Here a boy pushed down another just six hours ago and you tell me, there is no taint. Something strange is going on here....&quot; - &quot;Erh, no, my bad, the wyrm taint isn't the takeaway from this scene...:&quot;<br /> <br /> All in all, Sense Wyrm is used as a &quot;sense evil&quot; when on caern guard duty - for garou who return from away missions usually use the Rite of Cleansing before they approach the guards. If they hadn't had a chance or it didn't work, the warders discretion is applied. If garou are out on a mission however, Sense Wyrm is more an investigative tool. Anything that had contact with 'wyrmish' events could have taint, and with enough successes you might get clues what created the taint and so on. So it makes a nice story element and can lead to a huge problem if a player botches the sense wyrm roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T13:24:03-07:00","id":1440749,"title":"","content":"In Werewolf - Earthblood it seems spirits are harvested by posing next to them for a second, transfering energy. Then again, the Spirit Points are more like experience than what Gnosis is in the tabletop...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}